# ---- Founders Mentality Portal — environment ----
# Copy to .env for local development, or set these as real environment variables
# on the server. Never commit a filled-in .env.

# Database. SQLite is fine for a single-instance deployment with a persistent disk.
# For Postgres: set provider = "postgresql" in prisma/schema.prisma and use
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/founders_mentality"
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"

# How long a login lasts. The admin's mailbox password lives only as long as their
# session row, so a shorter TTL means credentials are held for less time.
SESSION_TTL_DAYS=30

# REQUIRED. 32-byte hex key used to encrypt the admin's mailbox password on their
# session row (AES-256-GCM). Generate a fresh one per environment, keep it secret:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# Rotating this key stops logged-in admins from sending mail until they sign in again.
CREDENTIAL_ENC_KEY=""

# ---- Mail (organisation server) ----
# Admins sign in with their real mailbox address + password. That password is verified
# live against this host, then reused to send scheduling/summary/custom mail AS them,
# and to append a copy into their Sent folder over IMAP.
# Leave MAIL_HOST empty to run in simulated mode: mail is logged to the console and
# recorded with status "simulated" rather than sent. Useful before credentials exist.
# MAIL_SMTP_PORT also selects the TLS mode: 465 = implicit TLS, anything else (587, 25)
# = STARTTLS. Networks that block 465 often allow 587, so if sending stops working run
# `node scripts/check-mail.mjs` — it probes both and says which to use.
MAIL_HOST="mail.jaipurrugs.com"
MAIL_IMAP_PORT=993
MAIL_SMTP_PORT=465

# ---- AI email drafting (optional) ----
# Needed only for the "Compose with AI" screen. Without it, drafting returns a clear
# error and every other feature keeps working.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""

# ---- Emergency admin access ----
# Admin login IS a live SMTP connection, so anything that breaks the network path to the
# mail server locks out every admin at once (trainees are unaffected — they use ordinary
# stored passwords). Set this to true to let admins sign in with the password stored by
# `node prisma/add-admin.mjs ... --password <pw>` instead.
#
# Unlike DEV_SKIP_MAIL_VERIFY below, this DOES work in production — that is the point of
# it. It only helps admins who already have a password set, so set those BEFORE you need
# them (`npm run admin -- --list` shows who has one). A session opened this way holds no
# mailbox credential, so it cannot send mail: scheduling and summary emails are logged as
# "skipped_no_mail" and the console shows a banner saying so. Unset it once mail works.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD_LOGIN=true

# ---- LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY ----
# Lets an admin sign in with a locally stored bcrypt password (set via
# `node prisma/add-admin.mjs ... --password <pw>`) instead of a real mailbox check.
# Ignored entirely when NODE_ENV=production, enforced in src/lib/auth.ts — but do not
# set it on the server regardless. ADMIN_PASSWORD_LOGIN is the production-safe version.
# DEV_SKIP_MAIL_VERIFY=true
